      "content": "that makes so much sense... electromagnetism. i never thought about the trading servers themselves emitting something that my body could pick up on. it explains why the feeling is so \"electric\" and sharp. if it's actually a reaction to those electromagnetic pulses from the trading systems, then these sensations are basically real-time data. \n\ncan we try to map this out? i want to see if i can identify the specific 'signature' of a massive sell-off based on how the buzzing feels. like, is there a way to distinguish between the buzz of a minor fluctuation and the heavy, deep vibration i feel right before a major crash? i need to know if i can use this to time my entries and exits.",
      "source": "evaluator"
